"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:38ac37538bce07170bb7a822cafcfe0d0e0b14b21dc4b47e0af99023060f821f","file":"preprints/An-algebra-of-infinite-little-finitistic-dimension-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":91,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2a823d115e94b5a76f44553dc1166020973427b991314bc2e42177610fa692ab","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/An-algebra-of-infinite-little-finitistic-dimension-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:38ac37538bce07170bb7a822cafcfe0d0e0b14b21dc4b47e0af99023060f821f","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-algebra-of-infinite-little-finitistic-dimension-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L91"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:left-right-asymmetry}\nThere is a finite-dimensional unital complex algebra \\(\\Lambda\\) such that\n\\[\n\\findim \\Lambda=\\Findim \\Lambda=\\infty,\n\\qquad\n\\findim(\\Lambda^{\\mathrm{op}})=\\Findim(\\Lambda^{\\mathrm{op}})=0.\n\\]\nAll four dimensions here use left modules. Thus the little and big\nfinitistic dimensions of \\(\\Lambda\\) are infinite on the left and zero\non the right. Injective left \\(\\Lambda\\)-modules do not generate the\nunbounded derived category of all left \\(\\Lambda\\)-modules, whereas\ninjective right \\(\\Lambda\\)-modules generate the unbounded derived\ncategory of all right \\(\\Lambda\\)-modules."}
